Stage done: polls website (REQUEST.md) implemented.

Start:
  bash setup.sh          # verifies python3, creates data dir (stdlib only, no downloads)
  PORT=8000 bash run.sh  # serves http://127.0.0.1:$PORT in the foreground (exec python3 app.py)
  DATA_DIR (default ./data) holds polls.db (SQLite). Sample polls are seeded when the DB is empty.

Features (English UI, white background, navy components #000080):
  - Navy top navigation: Polls (/), Create Poll (/create), Results (/results); active item highlighted.
  - Polls list (/): cards with title, description, option/vote counts, "You voted" badge, Vote and View results buttons.
  - Vote (/polls/<id>): radio options, submit votes; one vote per poll per visitor (voter cookie + UNIQUE constraint).
    After voting, the form is replaced by "You voted for X" and a link to results.
  - Results (/polls/<id>/results): navy progress bars with vote counts and percentages, total votes.
  - Results overview (/results): bars for every poll.
  - Create Poll (/create): title, optional description, 2-20 options one per line; validation errors shown inline; duplicates removed.
  - 404 and 405 pages with a way back to the polls list.

Verified by running the server: all routes return expected status codes; voting, duplicate-vote
rejection, invalid-option rejection, validation errors, and poll creation work; HTML escaping works.
Server was started and stopped by its own PID only (no pkill/killall).

Files: app.py (server + pages), run.sh, setup.sh, .gitignore (data/, __pycache__/).
